{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778615906254,"sessionID":"ses_1e24500ddffecxwbM5GPvd2nk5","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"functions.task:15","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Search for syndrome PMIDs","prompt":"Search for PubMed articles or references that mention any of the following as synonyms for Bosma arhinia microphthalmia syndrome (OMIM:603457):\n1. \"Ruprecht Majewski syndrome\"\n2. \"Gifford-Bosma syndrome\"\n3. \"BAM syndrome\" (as an expansion of BAMS)\n4. \"Bosma syndrome\" (short form)\n\nTry to find specific PMIDs or verify these are recognized synonyms. Use web searches if needed. Return what you find about the validity of these as synonyms and any PMIDs you can locate.","subagent_type":"general"},"output":"task_id: ses_1e2406172ffeHQK30pV74LuHhK (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\nHere are my search results for each proposed synonym:\n\n## 1. \"Ruprecht Majewski syndrome\"\n**NOT a recognized synonym.**\n- PubMed exact phrase search returned the warning: `\"quotedphrasesnotfound\":[\"\\\"Ruprecht Majewski syndrome\\\"\"]`\n- The search fell back to broader terms about arhinia/microphthalmia but found **no articles** using this exact phrase.\n- No mention in OMIM, MONDO, Wikipedia, or GARD.\n\n## 2. \"Gifford-Bosma syndrome\"\n**NOT a recognized synonym.**\n- PubMed exact phrase search returned the warning: `\"quotedphrasesnotfound\":[\"\\\"Gifford-Bosma syndrome\\\"\"]`\n- Same as above — no articles use this exact phrase. PubMed defaulted to the general arhinia/microphthalmia literature.\n- No mention in OMIM, MONDO, Wikipedia, or GARD.\n\n## 3. \"BAM syndrome\" (as a full expansion of the abbreviation)\n**NOT a recognized standalone synonym.**\n- PubMed found only **2 results** for the exact phrase `\"BAM syndrome\"`: PMID:41451907 and PMID:40093464.\n- Both articles use **\"Bosma arhinia microphthalmia (BAM) syndrome\"**, where **BAM** is an abbreviation in parentheses, not a standalone name.\n- MONDO already correctly lists **\"BAMS\"** as an `EXACT ABBREVIATION [OMIM:603457]`.\n- No evidence supports adding \"BAM syndrome\" as a separate name (it is only used parenthetically within the full name).\n\n## 4. \"Bosma syndrome\" (short form)\n**IS a recognized synonym with solid PMID support.**\n- PubMed exact phrase search found **6 articles** with specific PMIDs:\n  - **PMID:26842768** (2016) — explicitly states: *\"Bosma arhinia microphthalmia syndrome (Bosma syndrome)(OMIM 603457)\"*\n  - **PMID:38555111** (2024) — states: *\"The Bosma syndrome (BAMS: Bosma arhinia microphthalmia syndrome)\"*\n  - **PMID:38713859** (2025) — states: *\"congenital arhinia-microphthalmia syndrome or BOSMA syndrome\"*\n  - **PMID:37334829** (2023) — refers to *\"Bosma syndrome\"* in text\n  - **PMID:25573243** (2015) — lists *\"Bosma syndrome\"* among craniofacial syndromes in a review\n  - **PMID:16353241** (2006) — uses *\"Bosma syndrome\"* extensively throughout the article\n- Wikipedia also lists it: *\"Bosma syndrome\"* as an alternative name.\n\n## Summary\n\n| Proposed Synonym       | Valid? | PMIDs / Evidence |\n|------------------------|--------|------------------|\n| Ruprecht Majewski syndrome | No | None — exact phrase not found in PubMed |\n| Gifford-Bosma syndrome     | No | None — exact phrase not found in PubMed |\n| BAM syndrome               | No | Only used parenthetically as abbreviation (BAM); MONDO already has **BAMS** |\n| Bosma syndrome             | **Yes** | PMID:26842768, PMID:38555111, PMID:38713859, PMID:37334829, PMID:25573243, PMID:16353241 |\n\nThe only synonym with clear support in the peer-reviewed literature is **\"Bosma syndrome\"**, which could be added to MONDO with the PMIDs above as citations.\n</task_result>","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_1e2406172ffeHQK30pV74LuHhK","model":{"modelID":"moonshotai/Kimi-K2.6","providerID":"togetherai"},"truncated":false},"title":"Search for syndrome PMIDs","time":{"start":1778615557790,"end":17