{"type":"text","timestamp":1778616519793,"sessionID":"ses_1e24500ddffecxwbM5GPvd2nk5","part":{"id":"prt_e1dce09360011zhMWP50kYJTy7","messageID":"msg_e1dcdded5001GDYQlLtq6niVqp","sessionID":"ses_1e24500ddffecxwbM5GPvd2nk5","type":"text","text":"I have completed the work for **issue #9882**.\n\n### What I did\n\n1. **Checked out** `MONDO:0011323` for editing.\n2. **Researched** each requested synonym via PubMed and existing database cross-references (OMIM, Orphanet, GARD).\n3. **Added verified exact synonyms**:\n   - `\"arhinia, choanal atresia, microphthalmia, and hypogonadotropic hypogonadism\"` — sourced to `OMIM:603457`\n   - `\"Bosma syndrome\"` — sourced to `PMID:26842768` and `OMIM:603457`\n4. **Added** a term tracker item (`IAO:0000233`) pointing to issue #9882.\n5. **Ran ODK normalization** (`make NORM`) and **validated OBO syntax** with `robot convert`.\n\n### What I did NOT add (and why)\n\n- **\"Ruprecht Majewski syndrome\"** and **\"Gifford-Bosma syndrome\"** — No hits in PubMed, OMIM, GARD, or Orphanet.\n- **\"BAM syndrome\"** — Not found as a standalone name in literature; `BAMS` already exists as an exact abbreviation.\n- **\"Arhinia, choanal atresia, and microphthalmia\"** — Already the primary term label.\n- **\"Hyposmia-nasal and ocular hypoplasia-hypogonadotropic hypogonadism syndrome\"** — Already present.\n\n### Files created\n\n- `ISSUE_COMMENTS.md` — Feedback for the originating issue, explaining which synonyms were added and which could not be verified.\n- `PR_COMMENTS.md` — Human-readable description of the changes, rationale, and completed checklist.\n\n### Commit\n\n- `mondo-edit.obo` has been **committed locally** (`1453bbd`).","time":{"start":1778616502582,"end":1778616519792}}}
